deep.reconstruction:
Setting, from this page and its neighbours. The previous page fixes an additive category B (karoubian, 'Karoubi-closed', or simply abelian) and a class Σ of short exact sequences, in effect an exact structure in Quillen's sense (1972/73). From Σ it defines:
- Σ-monomorphisms and Σ-epimorphisms;
- Σ-strict morphisms: A→B factors as A→R→B, with A→R a Σ-epi and R→B a Σ-mono. Grothendieck calls R the 'Σ-moyenne' (Σ-middle term, i.e. the Σ-admissible image);
- Σ-projective and Σ-injective objects;
- Σ-special complexes: each differential is Σ-strict and the pieces (Ker, Im, Coim, H) fit into short sequences in Σ;
- Σ-acyclic complexes and Σ-resolutions: C^i = 0 for i<0 and H^i = 0 for i≠0.

On the source side there is a model k-linear exact category (P., Σ.). The next page shows its shape:
- Ψ^i. is k placed in degree i;
- each C^i. sits in a sequence 0→Ψ^i.→C^i.→Ψ^{i+1}.→0 in Σ., so C^i. behaves like the elementary contractible 'disk' complex in degrees i, i+1;
- every L. in P. is an iterated extension of objects (Ψ^i.)^{β_i}, via the stupid (degree) filtration, with Gr_i L. ≅ Ψ^i. ⊗ L_i;
- the C^i. are Σ.-projective.
So P. is a category of finite free graded objects or complexes over k, with degreewise split sequences as Σ.. It carries a tautological complex C^·. = (C^0.→C^1.→…), whose differentials factor through the Ψ^{i+1}. (the Σ.-moyennes). This complex is a Σ.-resolution of Ψ^0..

What the page wants to prove ('Il faudrait prouver'). Let Hom_{k,Σ-ex}(P.,B) be the k-linear functors P.→B sending Σ. to Σ. Inside it take the full subcategory of those commuting with Σ-moyennes; the next page calls the two classes Σ-sex and Σ-ex.
(a) Evaluation on the universal complex, F ↦ F(C^·.), maps Hom_{k,Σ-(s)ex}(P.,B) to B^· (cochain complexes in B). It is fully faithful. Its essential image is the complexes whose differentials d^i: C^i→C^{i+1} admit Σ-moyennes, i.e. are Σ-strict. In other words, (P., C^·., Σ.) is universal among triples (B, C^·, Σ) with such a complex, morphisms being Σ-exact functors.
(b) On the smaller class of functors, the essential image is exactly the Σ-resolutions: Σ-special complexes with H^i = 0 for i>0. So (P., C^·., Σ.) is the universal exact k-category equipped with a Σ-resolution.

Proof strategy (next page): dévissage of every object of P. into the Ψ's, which are moyennes of the C's, plus Σ-projectivity of the C^i.. This gives full faithfulness. One then constructs inverse functors B^·_{Σ-sex}→Hom_{Σ-sex}(P.,B) and B^·_{Σ-ex}→Hom_{Σ-ex}(P.,B).

Purpose. This is a 'classifying exact category' for resolutions. It lets one treat constructions on resolutions or perfect complexes (determinants, multiplicative structures, dévissage of ∂-perfect semi-simplicial complexes, as in the cote title) as universal constructions on the single model P.. Results then transfer to any exact category by Σ-exact functors, much as Dold–Kan-type or 'free' categories are used.
